---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { href, site } from "../lib/site";

const API = "https://devops-portfolio-microservice.vercel.app";

const bugs = [
  {
    title: "A time series that crashed for ten minutes every hour",
    symptom: "The metrics endpoint returned 500 whenever the current UTC minute was smaller than the number of points requested.",
    cause:
      "The series was built by subtracting from the minute field of the current timestamp. At 19:03 with ten points, minute arithmetic went negative and strftime raised ValueError.",
    fix: "Build timestamps with timedelta offsets instead of editing the minute field, so no wall-clock value is ever computed by hand.",
    guard: "A test that walks every minute of an hour and asserts the payload shape stays valid.",
  },
  {
    title: "A settings bug that only appeared in production",
    symptom: "The container exited on start with a JSON decode error, while the same code ran fine locally.",
    cause:
      "pydantic-settings decodes list-typed fields as JSON before validators run. The deployment set ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://a,https://b, which is valid for pydantic but not for json.loads.",
    fix: "Disable settings decoding and split comma separated values in a before-validator that also accepts a real JSON array.",
    guard: "Tests for both a comma separated string and a JSON list, plus a plain wildcard.",
  },
  {
    title: "A CI job that failed before running a single step",
    symptom: "The security scan job failed during setup for two commits in a row, with no log output at all.",
    cause:
      "The action reference aquasecurity/trivy-action@0.28.0 does not exist, the project publishes v-prefixed tags. GitHub rejects the job while resolving actions, which is why nothing logged.",
    fix: "Pin v0.36.0, and read the check annotations rather than assuming the failure was environmental.",
    guard: "The scan runs inside the job that already has a working runner, so a bad reference cannot orphan a whole job.",
  },
];

const evidence = [
  { value: "60", label: "pytest cases", note: "every route, error shape, CORS preflight and the GitHub mapping" },
  { value: "3", label: "Python versions", note: "3.11, 3.12 and 3.13 in the matrix" },
  { value: "5", label: "CI jobs", note: "lint, three test jobs, image build with scan and smoke test" },
  { value: "1", label: "real pipeline source", note: "the dashboard reads its own workflow runs, not invented ones" },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Case study | Rintu Chowdory"
  description="What this project is, what constrained it, what went wrong, and what the evidence actually proves. A DevOps case study with the failures left in."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-300">Case study</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">
      A portfolio that reports on itself
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-400">
      Most portfolio projects show a screenshot of a green pipeline. This one reads its own
      workflow runs from the GitHub API, so the numbers on the dashboard are the numbers of the
      build that produced the page.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <a class="btn btn-sm border-0 bg-white text-[#05080f] hover:bg-slate-200" href={href("/dashboard")}>Live dashboard</a>
    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline border-white/25 text-white hover:bg-white/10" href={href("/architecture")}>Architecture</a>
    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost text-slate-300" href={`${API}/docs`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Swagger</a>
  </div>

  <!-- PROBLEM -->
  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <article class="glass-panel p-5">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-300">The problem</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        I had repositories with tests and a Dockerfile, and nothing that proved either. A reader had
        to trust a README. Worse, the first version of the dashboard showed six services, three
        pipelines and nearly five thousand requests per minute that had never happened. Any engineer
        spots invented telemetry in about thirty seconds.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="glass-panel p-5">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-300">Constraints</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <li>No budget. Free tiers only, which rules out a managed cluster.</li>
        <li>The hosting account was already at its limit for free container services.</li>
        <li>No real traffic, so latency figures had to be either measured or labelled as demo.</li>
        <li>Every claim on the site has to be checkable by a stranger in a terminal.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="glass-panel p-5">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-300">The bet</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        Fix one thing properly: make the CI data real. Real runs have real failures, real durations
        and real awkward states like a run that fails before it starts. That is worth more than a
        dozen decorative panels, and it forces the API to handle rate limits, cold starts and
        partial outages the way a production service has to.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <!-- EVIDENCE -->
  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">The evidence</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {evidence.map((item) => (
        <div class="glass-panel p-5">
          <div class="mono text-3xl font-bold text-white">{item.value}</div>
          <div class="mt-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-300">{item.label}</div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-500">{item.note}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="glass-panel mono mt-4 overflow-x-auto p-5 text-xs text-slate-400">
      <div class="text-slate-500"># everything below is public, no login</div>
      <div class="mt-2">curl -s {API}/health</div>
      <div>curl -s {API}/api/v1/pipelines | jq '.source, .pipelines[0].service'</div>
      <div>curl -s {API}/metrics | head -20</div>
      <div>curl -s {API}/api/v1/services/nope</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BUGS -->
  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Three bugs worth keeping in the story</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-400">
      None of these were caught by reading the code. Each one now has a test or a structural fix
      behind it, which is the part that matters.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-5 space-y-4">
      {bugs.map((bug, index) => (
        <article class="glass-panel p-5 sm:p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="mono mt-0.5 text-xs text-slate-600">0{index + 1}</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">{bug.title}</h3>
              <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-3 text-sm text-slate-400 sm:grid-cols-2">
                <div>
                  <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Symptom</dt>
                  <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed">{bug.symptom}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Cause</dt>
                  <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed">{bug.cause}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">Fix</dt>
                  <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed">{bug.fix}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80">Guard</dt>
                  <dd class="mt-1 leading-relaxed text-emerald-100/80">{bug.guard}</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LIMITS -->
  <section class="mt-12 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="glass-panel p-5 sm:p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">What this does not prove</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <li>No production traffic, so the latency and uptime figures on the dashboard are demo data and labelled that way.</li>
        <li>No cluster. The Kubernetes panel describes namespaces that do not exist yet.</li>
        <li>One person, short history: there is no on-call rotation, no incident review and no scale story.</li>
        <li>A single region, a single environment. Promotion gates are on the roadmap, not in the repo.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
        Saying this out loud is the point. A portfolio that hides its limits reads like marketing.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="glass-panel p-5 sm:p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">What I would do next</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <li><span class="text-slate-200">Postgres instead of the in-memory store</span>, with Alembic migrations, so pipeline history survives a deploy.</li>
        <li><span class="text-slate-200">A load test in CI</span> with an SLO threshold, published as a chart, so "p95 under 200 ms" becomes a claim measured on every push.</li>
        <li><span class="text-slate-200">Signed images and Dependabot</span>, closing the supply-chain gap between a scanned image and a trusted one.</li>
        <li><span class="text-slate-200">Helm chart against kind</span>, with screenshots, and a real cluster only when one can be paid for.</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="mt-5 inline-block text-sm text-indigo-300 hover:text-white" href={href("/roadmap")}>See the roadmap</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a class="btn border-0 bg-white text-[#05080f] hover:bg-slate-200" href={href("/projects")}>The repositories</a>
    <a class="btn btn-outline border-white/25 text-white hover:bg-white/10" href={site.repoWebsite} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Site source</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost text-slate-300" href={site.repoMicroservice} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">API source</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
